From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm lanes: TF_GLM_OVN_MULTI_FILL batched prompt passes take marked and resumed prompts

Ported from ai-engine fork-ssh/ovn-up's ovn-batchresume (MULTI_FILL landed
2026-10-29 in 32060d706; plan(), the host tests and glm-multifill-check in
23062bd9c, merged 93dfbf29a). The current series keeps upstream's
prefill_many (fresh whole prompts in one pass) but refuses a resumed prompt
there, so several short suffixes off one kept state fill one at a time.

TF_GLM_OVN_MULTI_FILL: each pass takes every unfinished prompt's next piece,
from where it stands (0, a kept state it resumes, or its last piece's end) to
its next kept-state mark or its end, shortest first, up to prompt_rows, until
every prompt's first token is drawn. A piece starting at a mark fires it
first, the gate carries the kept state to the other ranks, and one forward
runs every piece's rows (cuda_prompt_pieces), then each piece's drafter rows,
its first token at its prompt's end, the head pass and the commit.
Admission needs the batched step vtable, so the package also carries the
stepped many vtable (many_rows + prefill_many, TF_GLM_PROMPT_MANY) it extends
with many_resumed: both knobs default off, and an arm sets PROMPT_MANY=1 for
the fresh-only pass or MULTI_FILL=1 for pieces.

Text edited from the fork: the series' chunk grid is prompt_cuts.nextCut rather
than the fork's chunkEnd, admits() also refuses a request with cuts, and the
mark context is the shared store's Keeps (the series' marksOf signature). The
GPU check compares batched against solo on first token, window tokens, logits
and position (the fork's held-state image needs the disk packages, which are
not part of the engine series).

Receipts: host tests of cut, plan (order, cap, marks, finished streams) and
admits, of the wire packet, and glm-multifill-check (GPU) for the passes.

